registered Futures Commission Merchant (Foris DAX FCM LLC or OG.com Broker). \n\nOG.com Markets offers both prediction market event contracts (Prediction Markets Contracts), as well as margined derivatives, including single stock futures and perpetuals (Futures) (Prediction Markets Contracts and Futures are collectively referred to as OG.com Markets Products). Prediction Markets Contract can be accessed directly on OG.com Markets or through a CFTC-registered FCM, including OG.com Broker, or an Introducing Broker (IB). Futures must be accessed through a CFTC-registered FCM, including OG Broker or an IB. \n\nTrading OG.com Markets Products involves risk and may not be appropriate for all. By trading you risk losing your cost to enter any transaction, including fees. You should carefully consider whether trading OG.com Markets Products is appropriate for you in light of your investment experience and financial resources. Any trading decisions you make are solely your responsibility and at your own risk.\n\nTo the extent an OG.com Markets Products references an agency, data or pricing source, index, or other measure, such reference does not indicate an endorsement of this tradeable financial instrument. Further, because such products are CFTC-regulated products, OG.com Markets may provide specific information related to the league or team such products apply to for full disclosure purposes only.\n\nOG.com is organized, registered, and operated in the United States. The information on this site is not directed at residents outside of the United States and is not intended for distribution to, solicitation of, or use by, any person in any country or jurisdiction where such distribution or use would be contrary to local law or regulation. None of the material on OG.com is to be construed as a solicitation, recommendation or offer to buy or sell any financial instrument on OG.com or elsewhere. \n\nOG.com Markets and OG.com Broker are subject to U.S. regulatory oversight by the CFTC. In order to trade OG.com Markets Products, a user must either become a Participant on OG.com Markets, a Customer of an Executing Broker (e.g. OG.com Broker or another FCM or IB) pursuant to the OG.com Markets rules (see below) and consent to the jurisdiction of OG.com Markets.\n\n\"Takes\", \"Pros play\", \"Call your shots\" are all phrases unique to OG.com wherein a Customer exercises discretion to trade CFTC-regulated event contracts. \"Parlay\" is a term unique to OG.com wherein a Customer requests a trade composed of a combination of specified events. OG.com uses various terms, including, but not limited to: Odds; Action; Chance; No Limits; Win; Multiplier; Sharp; Cover; Favorite; Prop Trading; Player Prop; Hit; Hit a Winning Trade; Moneyline; Play; Edge, that have meanings related to the trading of Prediction Markets Contracts.\n\nTo the extent market data on volume or open interest is provided in the OG.com Web and App, every effort is made to provide it on a near real-time basis, however, based on market activity such market data may be subject to delay, please consult end of day market data for final market data results.\n\nThe purpose of this website is solely to display information regarding the products and services available on OG.com. It is not intended to offer access to any of such products and services. You may obtain access to such products and services on OG.com Web and App. Please note that the availability of the products and services on OG.com is subject to jurisdictional limitations. OG.com may not offer certain products, features and/or services on the OG.com in certain jurisdictions due to potential or actual regulatory restrictions.\n\nContract specifications are available here. \nImage credits are available here. \nOG.com rules are available here.\nRisk disclosure is available here.\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"64:[\"$\",\"$L63\",null,{\"fallbackData\":{\"commodities_contract_spec\":\"https://www.nadex.com/contract-s